1nt1|n|A thin strip of wood, having the ends brought together, forming a somewhat elliptical hoop, across which a network of catgut or cord is stretched. It is furnished with a handle, and is used for catching or striking a ball in tennis and similar games. ; A variety of the game of tennis played with peculiar long-handled rackets; -- chiefly in the plural. ; A snowshoe formed of cords stretched across a long and narrow frame of light wood. ; A broad wooden shoe or patten for a man or horse, to enable him to step on marshy or soft ground. ; Confused, clattering noise; din; noisy talk or sport. ; A carouse; any reckless dissipation.	a:1249,12,2~1249,12,2	n:219n,120,4~219n,120,4	N:zf7,75,3;sjp,35,3;kco,26,2;273t,9,1~zf7,75,3;sjp,35,3;kco,26,2;273t,9,1
